  "body": "**[Original report](https://bitbucket.org/agriggio/art/issues/211) by Paul Matthijsse (Bitbucket: [Paul Matthijsse](https://bitbucket.org/Paul Matthijsse), ).**\n\n----------------------------------------\n\nThis is on Xubuntu 20.04 with Xfce\n\nCrop tool. \n\nTOOLBAR\\_TOOLTIP\\_CROP;<b>Crop</b> selection.\\\\nShortcut: <b>Shift-c</b>\\\\nMove the crop using <b>Shift</b>\\+<b>mouse drag</b>\\\\nResize the crop using <b>Ctrl</b>\\+<b>mouse drag</b>.\n\nShift\\+mouse drag does nothing, just mouse drag to move the crop.\n\nResize Ctrl\\+mouse drag: makes a new crop instead of a resize. Just resize by moving the crop borders.\n\nInfo key. \n\nIn Edit window, the I key no longer shows some basic info like file name and iso. Has unexpectedly changed to Shift\\+i. \n\nIn Inspector window, hitting the I key toggles the info below the thumbnails, as does Shift\\+I. No info about the opened photo.\n",
